So, I've never had much luck with barbarians, but I'm trying to
ascend all of the classes, and that's what the RNG gave me. So...
after a very harrowing early game, I've managed to get Cleaver, 
Stormbringer, crowned (I should have done something to reduce my
luck before doing that water prayer...), and some decent, but not 
great, armor. 

I'm confident in my ability to get most things, but I'm torn about
what weapons to use, both melee and at range. Barbarians can't get 
past basic with any ranged weapon except spear, and I don't think
you can throw multiple spears at once. Even if you can, they are
three times as heavy as daggers...

I have Axe at Expert and so Cleaver is a natural choice, but 4 points
of my AC are coming from a +3 orcish shield I ran into, and the extra 
damage is not worth it to me in exchange for the AC. It might be later
in the game if I'm at AC -40 anyway, but right now I think the AC is
more important. 

The last few games I've played, I have had access to some powerful 
missile weapon, and used that primarily. I mostly went back to melee
in the late game --- I can be a lot sloppier once I'm kitted out,
I find --- but daggers or a bow are what got me to that point to
begin with. Even the knight I ascended threw daggers and jumped 
around with the lance, and once I got the Mirror, it was magic missile
all the way. 

Barbarians, though... right now I'm throwing daggers, one per turn,
and then killing things when they walk up. I'm wielding Stormbringer
with some enchantment, because the level drain is useful, and I just
like Stormbringer. I can't come up with any better strategy than that,
but before I proceed forward (I've got the luckstone from the mines and
"oR from Sokoban, but haven't gone below DL10), I wanted to ask about it.

I'm also curious what people think the best thing to do is, going
forward; my inclination is Stormbringer and silver saber, twoweaponed,
because that's what I did with my rogue, and it worked great. I won't
have nearly as much skill, though, which makes me wonder if there is a
better option.  At this point I won't be guaranteed another artifact if
I try to wish for it, though if I altar camp enough I can probably get
something else.  I can get skilled in Longsword, but I can also get to
skilled with Stormbringer... I could get expert with hammer, if I wished
up Mojo or found it in a bones file, but I can't be guaranteed that,
plus I'd prefer not to destroy items if I can avoid it. 

Anyway, I think that if I play well otherwise, none of this will keep
me from ascending, but (a) that's a big if and (b) the easier I make
it on myself, the better. All comments and advice appreciated. 

